    {
      "tag": "pr-560",
      "title": "Retain compositor resources when GPU completion is unconfirmed",
      "summary": "Finite fence waits can fail while submitted GPU work is still pending. Continuing or tearing down after that result can reset resources still in use or free image memory before completion. This adds a terminal completion-unknown state that stops further presentation and retains pending resources until the app process exits, while preserving the existing genuine-device-loss path.",
